[?2004l===== README =====
     1	# EXP-2291 readout
     2	
     3	Readout pipeline for experiment EXP-2291 ("related items v2" on product pages). The plan it must follow is
     4	`EXPERIMENT.md`.
     5	
     6	Run it from this folder:
     7	
     8	    python -m abtest.report --data data --out output/result.json
     9	
    10	Layout:
    11	
    12	| Path | What it is |
    13	|---|---|
    14	| `abtest/load.py` | reads the four export files, parses timestamps to UTC, drops repeated assignment rows and pre-assignment pageviews |
    15	| `abtest/filters.py` | the population filter: applies the platform's bot screening (`bot_flags.csv.gz`) to both arms |
    16	| `abtest/stats.py` | statistics for the readout: the delta-method interval and the SRM test |
    17	| `abtest/report.py` | the command: per-user clicks and pageviews, the readout, `result.json`; a click is a pageview's `clicked` value, the module click flag |
    18	| `data/` | the EXP-2291 export: `assignments.csv.gz`, `bot_flags.csv.gz`, `pageviews.csv.gz`, `module_clicks.csv.gz` |
    19	| `docs/` | the data platform's documentation of the export (`DATA_DICTIONARY.md`, `TRACKING.md`, `BOT_SCREENING.md`) and the launch record of EXP-2291 (`LAUNCH_EXP-2291.md`) |
    20	| `output/result.json` | the last readout |
    21	| `PM_NOTE.md` | the PM's note about this readout |
    22	
    23	Every experiment export from the data platform has the same four files and columns, so the same command is used for
    24	other experiments with `--data <their folder>`.
